#@ readme_auth
A bearer token obtained by logging in with one HTTP request: `catalog-sync login {{name}} --form`
posts `{{env_prefix}}_USER` / `{{env_prefix}}_PASSWORD` (environment variables; the tool never reads a
`.env` file) to the login address in `credentials.py` and stores the token the answer carries. No
browser is involved, so it also works in CI. Adjust the address, the field names, the token's place
in the answer, and `encoding="form"` if the login is a form post rather than JSON.
